<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<!--
  Caste-restricted work, the soft way. Suggestion 2.3.

  Colors are confined to their caste's trade by law. NOT as incapables - a Red who
  cannot research is a worse pawn and it is wrong anyway; Reds are denied education,
  not unable. As a thought: a hierarchy believer working outside their Color's trades
  feels it, and an equality believer feels the opposite.

  Which trades belong to which Color is a CasteWorkExtension on each XenotypeDef
  (XenotypeDefs_Colors.xml), read by Source/RimRising/CasteLabor.cs (UNBUILT; until the
  DLL is rebuilt the two workerClass names below do not exist and these ThoughtDefs
  error on load - docs/Opus-Notes.md lists them first).

  STRUCTURE mirrored from Precepts_ColorDeference.xml in this folder: an IssueDef,
  one precept per meme with PreceptComp_SituationalThought, Thought_Situational
  ThoughtDefs with a RimRising worker. Both precepts are REQUIRED on their meme
  (Memes_RimRising.xml requireOne), per the associatedMemes lesson.

  Only the pawn's own feeling is modelled. The suggestion's observer thought ("a Red
  at the research bench") would be a social thought keyed on another pawn's current
  job, which is the ladder thought's shape and can be added the same way later.
-->
<Defs>

  <IssueDef>
    <defName>RR_CasteLabor</defName>
    <label>caste labor</label>
    <iconPath>UI/Issues/RR_CasteLabor</iconPath>
  </IssueDef>

  <ThoughtDef>
    <defName>RR_Thought_WorkOutsideCaste</defName>
    <thoughtClass>Thought_Situational</thoughtClass>
    <workerClass>RimRising.ThoughtWorker_CasteLabor</workerClass>
    <validWhileDespawned>false</validWhileDespawned>
    <stages>
      <li>
        <label>work above my station</label>
        <description>This is not my trade. It was never meant to be, and everyone who sees me at it knows it.</description>
        <baseMoodEffect>-4</baseMoodEffect>
      </li>
    </stages>
  </ThoughtDef>

  <ThoughtDef>
    <defName>RR_Thought_WorkBeyondCaste</defName>
    <thoughtClass>Thought_Situational</thoughtClass>
    <workerClass>RimRising.ThoughtWorker_CasteLabor_Equality</workerClass>
    <validWhileDespawned>false</validWhileDespawned>
    <stages>
      <li>
        <label>doing what I was never allowed</label>
        <description>They had a law about who could do this. Look at me doing it.</description>
        <baseMoodEffect>3</baseMoodEffect>
      </li>
    </stages>
  </ThoughtDef>

  <!-- What a believer thinks of SOMEONE ELSE doing another Color's work
       (ThoughtWorker_CasteLaborObserved), shaped like RR_Thought_ColorRank. -->
  <ThoughtDef>
    <defName>RR_Thought_SawWorkOutsideCaste</defName>
    <thoughtClass>Thought_SituationalSocial</thoughtClass>
    <workerClass>RimRising.ThoughtWorker_CasteLaborObserved</workerClass>
    <validWhileDespawned>false</validWhileDespawned>
    <stages>
      <li>
        <label>doing another Color's work</label>
        <description>That is not their trade, and they are doing it anyway, in front of everyone.</description>
        <baseOpinionOffset>-8</baseOpinionOffset>
      </li>
    </stages>
  </ThoughtDef>

  <PreceptDef>
    <defName>RR_CasteLabor_Confined</defName>
    <issue>RR_CasteLabor</issue>
    <label>each to their trade</label>
    <description>A Color is a function. The Reds dig, the Oranges build, the Yellows heal, the Golds rule, and a person doing another Color's work is a part in the wrong machine. It will not run well, and it will not be allowed to run long.</description>
    <impact>Medium</impact>
    <displayOrderInIssue>10</displayOrderInIssue>
    <associatedMemes>
      <li>RR_ColorHierarchy</li>
    </associatedMemes>
    <conflictingMemes>
      <li>RR_ColorEquality</li>
    </conflictingMemes>
    <comps>
      <li Class="PreceptComp_SituationalThought">
        <thought>RR_Thought_WorkOutsideCaste</thought>
        <description>Working outside one's Color</description>
      </li>
      <li Class="PreceptComp_SituationalThought">
        <thought>RR_Thought_SawWorkOutsideCaste</thought>
        <description>Someone working outside their Color</description>
      </li>
    </comps>
  </PreceptDef>

  <PreceptDef>
    <defName>RR_CasteLabor_Open</defName>
    <issue>RR_CasteLabor</issue>
    <label>any hands</label>
    <description>Every trade is open to every hand that can learn it. The Society said otherwise for eight hundred years and built its whole order on the lie; every Red at a research bench is a brick out of the wall.</description>
    <impact>Medium</impact>
    <displayOrderInIssue>20</displayOrderInIssue>
    <associatedMemes>
      <li>RR_ColorEquality</li>
    </associatedMemes>
    <conflictingMemes>
      <li>RR_ColorHierarchy</li>
    </conflictingMemes>
    <comps>
      <li Class="PreceptComp_SituationalThought">
        <thought>RR_Thought_WorkBeyondCaste</thought>
        <description>Working beyond one's Color</description>
      </li>
    </comps>
  </PreceptDef>

</Defs>
